# L §6.1 Joint models: `use a = "file" sha256 "..."` imports a closed model, pinned by its content (run with
# pin=bytes: the sha256 of the member file as the test gives it, E §3.1 step 1 leaving open what the hash is over);
# "its items are read as a.item (a.konto, a.tax[ola, 2025])"; "A member's asks are asked inside the joint model as a.q;
# since imports are pinned and never changed, joining changes no member's answer". The members are loaded under their
# prefixes (E §3.1 step 1) and read at the joint model's law date and cut. j1: ana's income for y plus ben's 80 000.00
# PLN: 180 000, 200 000, 210 000 PLN (num PLN, the def's type). j2: ana's tax[2026] = 120 000 * 0.12 = 14 400 PLN; a.q
# gives the same, as ana alone does; b.q is ben's income. A key of the joint's year index is a year (L §4.2 Keys as
# values), so it keys the member's year index. The register names the member's items and versions a.item, a.v. (The
# key 2026 is written in an ask: in a def it is a date literal in a rule, LOAD-LITERAL, L §7.1, in a joint model as in
# any.)
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "26a08dc22b514dc0b6eb7c1263103f06b216244b4ed980752bbc810412d05e45"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "a8bf3b260e60f625766da425a660f922557f525c28dcf8ed70567ec64d600ccc"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index jy = year 2025..2027

def income_sum[y in jy]: num PLN = a.income[y] + b.income at reader

ask j1: income_sum[y] for y in jy law 2026-12-31
ask j2: a.tax[2026] law 2026-12-31
ask j3: a.rate law 2026-12-31
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index yrs = year 2025..2027
input income[y in yrs]: money PLN
input rate: num
def tax[y in yrs]: num PLN = income[y] * rate at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2025..
  known 2025-01-01
  income[2025] = 100 000.00 PLN
  income[2026] = 120 000.00 PLN
  income[2027] = 130 000.00 PLN
  rate = 0.12

ask q: tax[2026] law 2026-12-31
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input income: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs 2025..
  known 2025-01-01
  income = 80 000.00 PLN

ask q: income law 2026-12-31
=== expect j1 j2 j3 a.q b.q
j1 (y = 2025): 180 000 PLN
  held: b.income = 80 000.00 PLN (b.v), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
j1 (y = 2026): 200 000 PLN
  held: b.income = 80 000.00 PLN (b.v), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
j1 (y = 2027): 210 000 PLN
  held: a.income[2027] = 130 000.00 PLN (a.v), read for 2027
  held: b.income = 80 000.00 PLN (b.v), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
j2: 14 400 PLN
  held: a.rate = 0.12 (a.v), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
j3: 0.12
  held: a.rate = 0.12 (a.v), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
a.q: 14 400 PLN
  held: rate = 0.12 (v), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
b.q: 80 000.00 PLN
  held: income = 80 000.00 PLN (v), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
